---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Website Monitor and SEO Checker — Signal
permalink: /signal/
softwareName: Signal website monitor
crumbSectionName: Signal
crumbSectionHref: /signal/
faq:
  - q: "What does Signal measure?"
    a: "Availability and HTTP status, response time, SSL validity and expiry, SEO and technical scores from a single fetch, and which analytics tools the page loads."
  - q: "Does it read my Google Analytics account?"
    a: "No. The analytics score reflects tracking scripts detected in the page markup only. It never connects to any analytics account."
  - q: "How often is a registered domain checked?"
    a: "On a schedule set by the operator, currently every five minutes, with every check stored as an event so the history builds over time."
  - q: "Why does the performance score differ from Vector?"
    a: "Both use the same analyzers, but response time is measured on each fetch and varies. The other scores should match between the two."
---
description: "Signal measures a domain now and keeps measuring it: uptime, response time, SSL, SEO and technical scores, and which analytics tools the site loads. Every number is a stored measurement."
---
{% set dim = dimensions[2] %}
{% set dimLede = "Enter a domain. Signal measures it now: availability, response time, SSL, SEO and technical scores, and the analytics tools it loads. Then it keeps checking on a schedule and stores every event." %}
{% include "partials/dimension-head.njk" %}

<section class="shell portfolio-section" data-signal>
  <form class="vector-form" data-signal-form novalidate>
    <label for="signal-url" class="label">Enter your domain</label>
    <div class="vector-inline__row">
      <input id="signal-url" name="url" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" placeholder="company.com" required aria-describedby="signal-help">
      <button type="submit" class="btn" data-signal-submit>Measure ↗</button>
    </div>
    <p id="signal-help" class="fine-print" data-signal-modenote>Public websites only. The domain is registered for scheduled checks so its history builds over time.</p>
    <p class="intake__error" data-signal-error role="alert"></p>
  </form>

  <div class="vector-state" data-signal-state="scanning" hidden aria-live="polite"><p class="overline">Measuring</p><ol class="vector-stages"><li data-state="active"><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Checking availability, response time, and SSL</li><li data-state="pending"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Reading the page for SEO, technical, and analytics signals</li><li data-state="pending"><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Storing the snapshot</li></ol></div>
  <div class="vector-state" data-signal-state="failed" hidden role="alert"><p class="overline">Measurement failed</p><h2 class="vector-state__title">The domain could not be measured.</h2><p class="vector-state__reason">Reason: <span data-signal-reason></span></p><button type="button" class="text-link" data-signal-reset>Try another domain ↗</button></div>
  <div class="vector-report" data-signal-state="result" data-signal-result hidden></div>

  <p class="overline" style="margin-top:56px">Monitored by the operator <span class="fine-print" data-signal-status></span></p>
  <div data-signal-board><div class="signal-empty" role="status"><p class="overline">Loading</p><h2>Reading stored checks…</h2></div></div>
  <div class="signal-feed" data-signal-feed><p class="overline" style="margin-top:44px">Events</p><div data-signal-events><p class="fine-print">Loading…</p></div></div>
</section>

<section class="pipeline-section" id="alerts"><div class="shell"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">How it works</p><h2>Scan now,<br>then keep measuring.</h2><p>A scan fetches the page once, runs the technical, SEO, performance, and content analyzers, and looks for analytics tools in the markup. The HTTP check and certificate read are the same ones the scheduler runs. Everything is stored as events, so a domain scanned today has a history next month.</p></div>
<ol class="engine-path" aria-label="Flow">{% for step in ["Domain","HTTP + SSL check","Analyzers","Analytics detection","Snapshot event","Scheduled checks"] %}<li><span class="project-type">{{ loop.index0 | pad }}</span><strong>{{ step }}</strong></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
<pre class="vector-console" aria-label="Rules">IF the check fails or returns 5xx      THEN status = unavailable → incident
IF status is 4xx or response &gt; 1500 ms  THEN status = degraded → warning
IF the certificate expires within 14 days THEN ssl warning
IF status returns to operational         THEN recovered</pre>
<p class="fine-print">The analytics score reflects which tracking tools the page loads. Signal does not read any analytics account; traffic figures would need Search Console or GA access and are not shown. Scores use Vector's documented scoring.</p></div></section>
